{"title":"2014 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Directly_solving_for_c)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Directly solving for c)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba70df5a2f9630194f32f50010cd2e78318c98d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b&lt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> be three integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> is an arithmetic progression and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/3/1c330d1138fdde755f13c54e34de11c2d0c4d680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,c,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is a geometric progression.  What is the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27fac67c3da012a3bcada3f79bfa5770f11b9dd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }-2\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }1\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }2\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }4\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }6\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/8278c99d5e9f42c042413525178c3c43a5f6390b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-a=c-b$\" width=\"102\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/a/b3a126e9a76abc1dddf2603ae4dcf6a88e943a82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2b-c$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/3/1c330d1138fdde755f13c54e34de11c2d0c4d680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,c,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is geometric, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5cf17d99e641497950e85c557bfbcfb10cd42bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2=ab=(2b-c)b \\Rightarrow 2b^2-bc-c^2=(2b+c)(b-c)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"448\" height=\"19\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba70df5a2f9630194f32f50010cd2e78318c98d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b&lt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />, we can't have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebda5306c70a24c574ef0107ed5b5152b5f594cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=c$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c0171205cc0ad7f4f811ef834bfd7b6af3e5f906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=-2b$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />. Then our arithmetic progression is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d4e83fb611021ac9fa73fb0123aa4c0308fc0c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4b,b,-2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/4048f34740c4357fc7ae8938e92df8286ed5d0a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4b &lt; b &lt; -2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/beab3b5c143f2b58c18e15cdb470a15386701dab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />. The smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c0171205cc0ad7f4f811ef834bfd7b6af3e5f906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=-2b$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08e49136687e2ed695ec26c96f71c5243ea7b4bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2)(-1)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>(Solution by AT)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Taking the definition of an arithmetic progression, there must be a common difference between the terms, giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/9061c58fcecf12c3bb40bf43291a67efc6299586.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b-a) = (c-b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" />. From this, we can obtain the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3dab9e38a3c4094dbf8d793bb15db08b274b488c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2b-c$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />. Again, by taking the definition of a geometric progression, we can obtain the expression, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8d2e709d34b7619da2e586ded31672af04f76b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=ar$\" width=\"49\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d40910a5e41a88bc61ca13f6ceaa68c4d2860ea1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=ar^2$\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />, where r serves as a value for the ratio between two terms in the progression. By substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> in the arithmetic progression expression with the obtained values from the geometric progression, we obtain the equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d98f859353e1f9924c4eef29fe5935732b3f6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2ar^2-ar$\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" /> which can be simplified to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b19f424d1cecc9c773d8d1c32c5737ea4ba4784.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r-1)(2r+1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" /> giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/1930619a38fceee8e02990ea79026a348193307e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fba02d8ac615a83812bbfc81f3de68c13efac077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=-1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, from the geometric progression, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/3/1a351eb298ff1526bb4bc134ed0a57e4a751b6be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=a$\" width=\"43\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c81d39ade559eee4198db4622d2c6b5422ee5887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1/4a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b585c82563a5199c70dbd9dac783ca07737550d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=-1/2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />. Looking at the initial conditions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba70df5a2f9630194f32f50010cd2e78318c98d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b&lt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> we can see that the lowest integer value that would satisfy the above expressions is if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/7/4776d545e58865e347c9c5d3991937c1cc143d98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = -4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />, thus making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f72da4187cb0ff8d0471bef17474df62fe69c94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" /> \n(Solution by thatuser)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the definition of an arithmetic progression, we can label the terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83c9c3a8da8388f2c9107e68f8fe59683cd0cdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b89e2225617aed18d1a3bb39906075c99699176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+2d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />. Now, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b89e2225617aed18d1a3bb39906075c99699176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+2d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83c9c3a8da8388f2c9107e68f8fe59683cd0cdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> form a geometric progression. Since a geometric ratio has a common ratio between terms, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/9/729a3e888c4d29ba6b461d8daad7ae2d6040f374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+2d)/a = (a+d)/a+2d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"222\" height=\"18\" />. Cross multiplying, we obtain the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4ea27139345d3ee7bb3aec8daeefc84925d48f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+2d)^2=a(a+d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"19\" />. Multiplying it out and cancelling terms, we are left with the quadratic equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/7/1c7166f1f3d4d9a953c20235f89710e2cb54b6d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4d^2+3ad=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f38fa78b71167027dae91e2b24d38171af0ed2fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=-3a/4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791662898215b138613f4dada0a3ce54193d735f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Looking at the problem, we know that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be 0, therefore the arithmetic progression is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6cb11fbd3e78b97d67be1fc9f6b6f93f958c756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, a/4, -a/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />, so we need to find the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52bce5b8ba3e90c6f47c5c114251d1d7312de4e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-a/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a2a2ba78a899722dbde1c6fefddda78fa19837.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-a/2&gt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />. Looking at our progression, we realize that a must be a multiple of 4 so that every term is an integer. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f59ef1b07d364c2ccf7077ea0d2ddf5fb05a7a33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />, since that would yield the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52bce5b8ba3e90c6f47c5c114251d1d7312de4e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-a/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> which satisfies the conditions, we figure out that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n(Solution by i8Pie)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Directly_solving_for_c.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Directly_solving_for_c)\">Solution 4 (Directly solving for c)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Directly solving for c)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the set-up in the second solution, we can obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb81480621cb40261584d9e80d59e87d4694b623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b=a+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fb782f3acc157bb4561454a864ede55cdb212af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2=ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />. Directly solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/583b392da8a4f16828a3f67a8f541fe72f0054e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2=a(\\frac{a+c}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"37\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc94a0193875f05a591937b233c2abba52e91fd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c^2-ac-a^2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />, a polynomial with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Solving using the quadratic formula yields results <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88ef873cad39a9f5931948b204f13802f0e1c8aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96b51037d4e0e1a27bbd7a0357a2c2a331e45711.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=-\\frac{1}{2}a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />. By definition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba70df5a2f9630194f32f50010cd2e78318c98d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b&lt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96b51037d4e0e1a27bbd7a0357a2c2a331e45711.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=-\\frac{1}{2}a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />. Solving for b yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c61f45447aa441e2cbcf4470e260046fd9bd87c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{a}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"34\" />. The rest follows solution 2 and gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f72da4187cb0ff8d0471bef17474df62fe69c94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />\n(Solution by cayleynotfermat1005)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/sxBuSZGfmHg\">https://youtu.be/sxBuSZGfmHg</a>\n</p><p>~Lucas\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid bl